# {ProjectName} — Web-Novel Writing Toolkit

## Skill Routing Table

| Command | Skill | Description |
|------|-------|------|
| `/story-long-write`、`/write-long` | story-long-write | Long-form web-novel writing (chapter by chapter) |
| `/story-short-write`、`/write-short` | story-short-write | Short-form web-novel writing (emotion-driven) |
| `/story-long-analyze`、`/teardown-long` | story-long-analyze | Long-form novel deep teardown |
| `/story-short-analyze`、`/teardown-short` | story-short-analyze | Short-form novel teardown analysis |
| `/story-long-scan`、`/scan-long` | story-long-scan | Long-form novel batch scanning |
| `/story-short-scan`、`/scan-short` | story-short-scan | Short-form novel batch scanning |
| `/story-deslop`、`/deslop` | story-deslop | Remove AI writing traces |
| `/story-cover`、`/cover` | story-cover | Generate cover art |
| `/story-review`、`/review` | story-review | Multi-perspective adversarial review |
| `/story-import`、`/import` | story-import | Import existing novels into the project structure |
| `/story`、`/webnovel` | story | Toolbox router · auto-dispatch of fuzzy intents |
| `/story-setup`、`/setup` | story-setup | Environment deployment · one-click deploy of hooks/rules/agents |
| `/browser-cdp` | browser-cdp | Browser CDP tool |

## File Structure

- `teardown-lib/` — teardown analysis output
- `{BookTitle}/prose/` — long-form novel prose chapters
- `{BookTitle}/setting/` — character settings, world settings
- `{BookTitle}/outline/` — volume outlines, chapter outlines
- `{BookTitle}/tracking/` — context.md (writing context), foreshadowing.md
- `{BookTitle}/benchmark/` — benchmark-book analysis

## Collaboration Rules

Coordination between agents is described by the responsibility-boundary sections of each agent definition file; no separate coordination-rules file is needed.

## Recovering Context After Compaction

This section takes effect automatically after compaction. CLAUDE.md is reloaded after every compaction.
Key writing context:
1. Current writing project name and progress
2. Recently discussed character-setting changes
3. List of unfinished foreshadowing
4. Current chapter's emotion/pacing targets

If {BookTitle}/tracking/context.md exists, read it first after compaction to restore context.
